    "description": "The only fixed key material in libsignal v0.99.1's test suites that touches PQXDH: a Kyber1024 (round 3, libsignal KEM type 0x08) key pair stored as raw files and used by the Rust tests test_serialize and test_kyber1024_kem in rust/protocol/src/kem.rs. The tests prepend the type byte 0x08, deserialize, and require byte-identical re-serialization; test_kyber1024_kem then encapsulates to the public key with fresh randomness and checks decapsulation agrees (no fixed ciphertext or shared secret exists upstream). libsignal has NO fixed PQXDH handshake vectors: every PQXDH test generates identity, signed, one-time, base and Kyber keys at runtime (see spec/protocol/pqxdh.md section 10). The spec agent additionally checked, with OpenSSL SHA3-256, that the secret key embeds the public key at byte offset 1536 and SHA3-256(public key) at offset 3104 (the round-3 Kyber expanded-secret-key layout described in spec/crypto/kem.md); those checks are recorded as derived fields.",
